# Fixed a typo here that made this file a no-op ("node_modelues") — never actually
# ignored anything.
node_modules/

# Frontend build output (server/web/src -> here via `npm run build`, vite.config.ts's
# outDir). Regenerable, was previously committed by mistake — the Dockerfile now builds
# it fresh from source (see server/Dockerfile's frontend-builder stage), so committing
# it is no longer needed for deploys, and a fresh clone must run `make web-build` (or
# `cd web && npm run build`) once before `make dev`/`make run` for local dev.
static/app/

# Compiled Go binary (Makefile's `make build` -> `go build -o toToogle main.go`; also
# written by a bare `go build ./...` from this directory, since Go drops a binary named
# after the module for every main package it finds under `./...`). Same mistake as
# static/app/ above — a binary was committed at some point (commit f4ee2ff) instead of
# being built fresh; removed and ignored here so it can't happen again.
/toToogle
